  data: {
    LLM: 'Focus on making your opening meld as soon as possible. Decide whether to draw 2 from stock or take the discard pile based on what you need. Start canastas early so you can go out later.\n\nCoordinate with partner on which canastas to pursue. The wild card canasta is valuable (2000 pts clean) but commits you - only start if you have many wilds. Track red 3s - having 4 is great (1000 pts), but 5 is bad (-600 penalty). Manage the discard pile - taking it gives many cards but may include unwanted points.\n\nComplex decisions about when to take the large initial discard pile. Timing your go-out to maximize bonuses or minimize opponent opportunities. Strategic freezing of the discard pile. Optimal allocation of wild cards between natural melds vs wild canasta attempt.',
